# A `_` parameter accepts an err and the body runs; a named parameter makes the
# call short-circuit as chapter 04 describes ("when one shows up as an
# argument, the function body never runs").
#
# Run from this directory: kanso run main.kso; kanso run main.kso --interp
#  (both show it)
#
# Expected: demo_a reports the err "boom 1" at the endpoint, like demo_b.
# Actual: demo_a prints "ignored body ran with 5" and "boom 1" is lost. Every
# engine agrees, so the failure disappears silently everywhere.
#
# Where it bit: a parser step `fn float_done tok _` whose second argument was
# the result of a validation step. The validation failed, the body ran anyway,
# and `text/to_float` raised a different, worse error about the same input.
fn boom n
  err "boom {n}"

fn ignores x _
  "ignored body ran with {x}"

fn binds x y
  "binding body ran with {x} {y}"

pub demo_a =
  e = boom 1
  ignores 5 e

pub demo_b =
  e = boom 2
  binds 5 e
